ubclass's built-in value; a bound method of a Python"] [100 2 "// function is called by pushing its frame"] [132 1 "// dictArgs are a keyword dictionary as a call's trailing keyword arguments."] [219 20 "// a dict subclass's __setitem__ sees the body's names (PY5e, part 2b)"] [250 1 "// updateBases resolves __mro_entries__ (PEP 560): the same tuple when no base has one."] [291 1 "// calculateMetaclass is _PyType_CalculateMetaclass: the most derived of meta and the bases' types."] [308 1 "// ---- type.__new__, type.__init__, type.__call__ ----"] [389 3 "// type_ready_set_dict's gh-55664"] [400 2 "// type_new_set_attrs comes before PyType_Ready: a metaclass's mro() sees __class__ set"] [407 2 "// __module__, __qualname__, __doc__"] [426 2 "// __new__ a staticmethod, __init_subclass__ and __class_getitem__ classmethods"] [435 2 "// __slots__ (type_new_slots)"] [454 32 "// type_dict_set_doc; a member named __doc__ is there already (typing's _SpecialForm)"] [456 2 "// __eq__ without __hash__ makes the class unhashable"] [464 2 "// __set_name__"] [476 2 "// __init_subclass__: super(type, type), whose check reads the MRO (a custom mro() may have left the class out)"] [498 1 "// checkLayouts refuses bases whose instance layouts conflict."] [509 1 "// bestBase is best_base: the base whose solid base is the most derived."] [527 1 "// c3MRO is the C3 linearization of t over its bases (mro_internal's mro_implementation)."] [586 1 "// mangle is _Py_Mangle: __x in class C is _C__x."] [609 1 "// ---- object.__new__, object.__init__ ----"] [611 1 "// overrides is a heap class of t's MRO defining name, or, for __new__, t's built-in solid base not"] [612 1 "// object (a built-in type's inherited slot cannot be told from its own: Go's functions do not compare)."] [623 4 "// a static type's tp_name is its module's and its name (select.poll)"] [669 25 "// its __del__ at its death (finalize.go, queue 218)"] [688 2 "// The data model's slots of object and type (REQUEST to PY5b: leave these to class.go)."] [701 1 "// ---- the slots of a class (fixup_slot_dispatchers, update_slot) ----"] [707 1 "// pyDefined is name defined by a heap class of t's MRO (a Python method), and its value."] [716 1 "// fixupSlots fills t's slots: the built-in solid base's (unwrapping a built-in subclass's value),"] [717 1 "// then a dispatcher for each special method a class of the MRO defines. Rerun on a class's"] [718 1 "// special attribute's assignment, for it and its subclasses."] [729 21 "// a custom mro() without object (typeNew refuses such a class afterwards)"] [745 4 "// dict's subscript sees the subclass's instance (its __missing__; dict's accessors take the"] [746 4 "// instance through BuiltinValueHook): PY5e, part 2b"] [870 4 "// slot_tp_call's _Py_EnterRecursiveCall (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's"] [871 4 "// test_recursive_call, A.__call__ = A(), overflowed Go's stack)"] [1040 1 "// reprOfInstance are the built-in types whose repr names the instance's own type (_PyType_Name(Py_TYPE(self)):"] [1041 1 "// deque's, defaultdict's): their subclasses' instances reach the Repr slot as they are, not unwrapped (PY7: a"] [1042 1 "// subclass's repr named the base)."] [1045 1 "// unwrapSlots makes a built-in base's slots work on its subclass's instances: each argument that is"] [1046 1 "// such an instance replaced by its value, and the base's __new__'s value wrapped in the instance."] [1114 1 "// wrapNew is a built-in __new__ called for a class deriving from it: its value in an instance."] [1123 1 "// wrapInstance is the instance of the heap class t that keeps the built-in value v (wrapNew's), tracked when t"] [1124 1 "// defines __del__ (queue 218)."] [1138 26 "// socket.socket's: sock_finalize at its death"] [1143 1 "// callSpecial calls o's special method name (looked up on its type, as CPython's lookup_maybe_method)."] [1149 2 "// the C level's recursion check (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_repr_as_str,"] [1150 2 "// __repr__ = __str